            "review_title": "Review at Lumiere Texas Bbq & Craft Beer",
            "review_text": "Dan T\n12 contributions\n0\nPub restaurant just next to Holiday Inn Airport Suite hotel.\nApr 2024 • Solo\nStaff was helpful and friendly however teo comments which I hope management will consider to improve. \n\n1. Happy hours should cover non-alcoholic drinks or mocktails as not everyone drinks alcohol. \n\n2. The steak should never be served together with the soup. I had to ask them to take the steak back while I finished my soup. By the steak was back (which was about 3mins later, I had to rush finishing my soup), the steak was already lukewarm so that wasn’t good. \n\nOn the plus side, the doneness (I asked for medium rare) was spot on so kudos to the chef. \n\nThe soup was more like a pumpkin soup than a real crab bisque so suggest they change it to vegetable cream soup with some crab meat.\nRead more\nWritten April 21, 2024\nJohn Walker\nThank you for your review. We’ll take note your feedback to improve our food quality as well as our services. Hope to see you again soon.\nWritten April 23, 2024\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
